--TEST--
`Core\Json::encodeEach` throws a `LogicError` for an element with a `secret` property, with the message `Core\Json::encode` gives under its own name —`rule:core-classes/json-whole-and-stream`, `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Json::encodeEach
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Login {
    public tainted string $user;
    public secret tainted string $password;

    public function constructor(tainted string $user, secret tainted string $password) {
        $this->user = $user;
        $this->password = $password;
    }
}

var $login = Core\Json::decodeAs<Login>('{"user":"ada","password":"pw-1"}');
array<mixed> $items = ["first", $login, "last"];

string $wholeMessage = "";
try {
    echo Core\Json::encode($items), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $whole) {
    $wholeMessage = $whole->message;
}

string $eachMessage = "";
try {
    foreach (Core\Json::encodeEach($items) as tainted bytes $piece) {
        echo "a piece was given\n";
    }
    echo "the secret was written\n";
} catch (LogicError $each) {
    $eachMessage = $each->message;
}
echo $wholeMessage, "\n";
echo $eachMessage, "\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Json::encode(): an instance of `Login` cannot be encoded, because its property `$password` is `secret`
Core\Json::encodeEach(): an instance of `Login` cannot be encoded, because its property `$password` is `secret`
